# kaneo_team_member

Manages one team relationship, identified by workspace, team, and user IDs. Changing any identifier replaces it. Existing relationships must be imported; Create does not adopt them.

## Example usage

{{ tffile "examples/resources/kaneo_team_member/resource.tf" }}

## Prerequisites and new teams

The operator needs accepted workspace membership and `member.update` to add members, `member.delete` to remove them. Instance admin access alone is insufficient. The target must already be an accepted workspace member. `kaneo_workspace_member` creates an invitation without waiting for acceptance. A dependency on that resource does not wait for acceptance either. Accept the invitation externally before applying team membership; use the actual user ID, not a workspace member ID or email.

New `kaneo_team` resources do not add their creator. Manage the operator's own `kaneo_team_member` explicitly, as above. Add `depends_on = [kaneo_team_member.operator]` to every other membership in that team. This orders creation after bootstrap and destruction before operator removal. Import the operator relationship if it already exists, including the workspace's seeded default team membership.

Normally, refresh and import require the operator to belong to the team. When the API denies listing, the provider checks the authenticated user ID and freshly checks workspace access and team presence. Only a target matching that authenticated user can be proven absent this way and recreated. For any other target, lost list access retains state and reports an error. The provider never implicitly adds the operator. If operator membership is removed out of band while other members are managed, restore it separately before a full apply. Terraform refresh runs before dependency-ordered creation.

