## Import

Import uses `workspace_id/team_id/user_id`. URL path-escape each native ID separately, then join with slashes. The representation must be canonical; empty IDs and whitespace are invalid. The computed ID uses the same format.

{{ codefile "shell" .ImportFile }}

Find team IDs with `/api/auth/organization/list-teams?organizationId=workspace-id` and user IDs with the workspace's authenticated member list. All three IDs must describe the same relationship.

## Deletion and recovery

Destroy removes only the specified team relationship. It does not change workspace access, invitations, roles, user accounts, or memberships in other teams. A stored orphan team row whose workspace membership is missing remains managed; removal reports an error until an operator repairs the upstream data or restores the prerequisite. The provider does not grant workspace access to repair it.

Refresh clears state only after proving relationship or scoped parent absence. Authentication errors, lost workspace access, malformed lists, duplicate rows or users, and unproven deletion errors retain state. Restore operator access before retrying. Every member row must be valid, even unrelated rows. Better Auth has no member-list pagination and caps results at 100; the provider refuses lists with 100 or more rows. Custom server filtering or lower caps can invalidate completeness assumptions.

If add succeeds but its response is lost or invalid, inspect the relationship and import its triple ID before retrying. A valid add response records state before confirmation so a failed confirmation can be reconciled. Concurrent adds can create duplicate rows upstream; avoid multiple writers. Independent invitation acceptance or another writer can recreate a removed membership. Deletion does not cancel invitations and cannot guarantee permanent absence.
